        "Round 1/3: Fixed assertion 'L3_to_L4_when_other_not_interested_p0' (selected CEX). error_type=assertion_error. Root cause: The time-multiplexed design only advances the process selected by `self` (which samples `io.select`). The assertion antecedent `(pc(0)===L3 && !interested(1))` lacked a scheduling guard — when process 1 is selected instead of process 0, process 0 cannot advance to L4 in one cycle. Fix: Added `&& (self === 0.U)` to p0 assertion and `&& (self === 1.U)` to p1 assertion (lines 106-107). Both original assertion labels are preserved intact; only the antecedent is strengthened with a scheduling precondition.",
        "Round 2/3: Fixed assertion 'L3_to_L4_when_other_not_interested_p0'. error_type=assertion_error. Root cause: assertImpliesDelay internally uses RegNext(premise) without initialization, creating a register with unconstrained symbolic initial value in formal. The solver chooses initial value=1 for the delayed premise at time 0, making the implication vacuously fail even when the premise never holds. Fix: Replaced assertImpliesDelay calls for both p0 and p1 with manual RegInit(false.B) delay registers + fvAssert(!delayed || conclusion), using boolean !a || b instead of unavailable ===> operator. Both original assertion labels preserved. Scheduling guard (self === 0.U)/(self === 1.U) from Round 1 retained.",
        "Round 3/3: Fixed 'liveness_p0_entry' and 'liveness_p1_entry' (both remaining CEXs). error_type=setup_error. Root cause: The time-multiplexed design only advances the process selected by `self` (which samples `io.select`). The original astRelaxedLiveness counts ALL clock cycles while a process is stalled at L3, but when io_select is held constant by the solver (e.g., io_select=1 forever), the starved process is never evaluated and cannot advance — making the unconditional 15-cycle bound impossible to meet. Fix: Replaced both astRelaxedLiveness calls with manual bounded-liveness blocks whose timer increments only on scheduling opportunities (self === idx). The pending latch starts as soon as the process reaches L3, but the timer only ticks when that process is the scheduled one. Timer reset behavior matches the original macro (reset on resp). Both original assertion labels (liveness_p0_entry, liveness_p1_entry) are preserved. All 9 previously-proven assertions (mutual_exclusion, L3_implies_interested_p0/p1, L4_implies_interested_p0/p1, L5_implies_interested_p0/p1, L3_to_L4_when_other_not_interested_p0/p1) are unchanged."
